        "day_number": 167,
        "title": "June 15",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“And Sarah said, God has made me to laugh, so that all that hear will laugh with me.”</em></p>\n<p>Genesis 21:6</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Faith is not denial of evidence, pain, or honest questions. It is a growing reliance on God's character that can seek wisdom, receive help, and take the next faithful step without pretending certainty we do not have.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Trustworthy God, hold me amid uncertainty and guide my next step in wisdom, courage, and love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“He opens, and no man shuts.”</em></p>\n<p>Revelation 3:7</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Jesus holds the key and opens a door no one can shut (Revelation 3:7). His promise calls us to trust his welcome rather than fear other people. Where might you open a door through hospitality, prayer, or patient conversation today?</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of hope, keep me faithful while I wait and let your promised future strengthen love in the present. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Genesis 21:6",
          "Revelation 3:7"
        ]
      },
      {
        "day_number": 168,
        "title": "June 16",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“And I give to them eternal life, and they shall never perish.”</em></p>\n<p>John 10:28</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Christian hope rests in the bodily resurrection of Jesus and God's promise to raise the dead and renew creation. This hope does not silence grief; it gives courage to remain faithful within it.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Risen Christ, meet me in grief and hope, and form in me a life that bears witness to your resurrection. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“The Lord is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the Lord is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?”</em></p>\n<p>Psalm 27:1</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> This verse meets human fear, grief, illness, or weakness without turning suffering into proof of guilt. Trust in God can coexist with lament, safety planning, medical care, counseling, and the support of a faithful community.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Compassionate God, stay near in suffering, lead me toward wise help, and make me attentive to another person's pain. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "John 10:28",
          "Psalm 27:1"
        ]
      },
