        "day_number": 343,
        "title": "December 8",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“You have a few names even in Sardis which have not defiled their garments; and they shall walk with me in white: for they are worthy.”</em></p>\n<p>Revelation 3:4</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Biblical hope is patient confidence in God's faithfulness, not a promise that every difficulty will quickly disappear. Let hope make room for honest lament and sustain one concrete act of love today.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of hope, keep me faithful while I wait and let your promised future strengthen love in the present. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“You, O God, have prepared of your goodness for the poor.”</em></p>\n<p>Psalm 68:10</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> God's concern for people who are poor, oppressed, excluded, or unheard calls for more than private sympathy. Notice whose dignity or safety is at stake, listen before acting, and join mercy to practical justice.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of justice and compassion, show me where love requires action, and give me courage to protect dignity and seek the good of my neighbor. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Revelation 3:4",
          "Psalm 68:10"
        ]
      },
